---
import BrandGuide from '../../components/BrandGuide.astro';
import AffLink from '../../components/AffLink.astro';
---

<BrandGuide
  brandKey="zara"
  brand="Zara"
  title="Zara Size Guide — Does Zara Run Small? (Charts & Tips) | Attirel"
  description="Zara runs small with a slim European cut, so most shoppers size up. Zara size charts for women and men with US, UK, and EU conversions, plus fitting tips."
  h1="Zara Size Guide"
  standardCharts={false}
  chartsHeading="Where Zara's measurements live"
  fitSections={[]}
  faqs={[]}
  related={[]}
>
  <Fragment slot="verdict">
    <strong>Yes — Zara runs small, with a slim European cut.</strong> Zara designs to
    continental European proportions: narrower shoulders, slimmer sleeves, and a shorter torso
    than typical US/UK brands. Most shoppers should size up at least one size, especially in
    blazers, shirts, and denim.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="charts-intro">
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
      Zara publishes no brand-level size chart. Measurements are stated per garment: select a size
      on <AffLink brand="zara">the product page</AffLink> and Zara shows the body measurements that
      size fits, alongside a per-item "Find your size" tool that takes your measurements and fit
      preference. Any brand-wide Zara chart you find elsewhere online is a third-party
      reconstruction, and they disagree with one another, so treat the product page as the only
      authority. (Per Zara's help centre, August 2026.)
    </p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="tips">
    <li><strong>Zara sizes by EU numbers first:</strong> the tag shows EU sizing with US/UK conversions printed underneath. When in doubt, trust the EU number and the garment measurements.</li>
    <li><strong>Blazers and outerwear:</strong> cut close through the shoulders, so size up if you layer underneath.</li>
    <li><strong>Denim:</strong> Zara jeans have minimal stretch in many lines; size up unless the listing says "stretch."</li>
    <li><strong>Between sizes?</strong> With Zara's slim cut, go up, not down.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the product page:</strong> Zara's fit varies noticeably between collections (TRF runs smaller than the main line).</li>
  </Fragment>
</BrandGuide>
